A||||30||88formula||How much do I pay?||||5
Z||000000||88formula||10-24-1999||03:34 PM||||I have the opportunity to purchase an 88 Pontiac Formula. The car is equipped with a five speed manual, air conditioning, sun roof, power windows, and it only has 48K original miles on it.The car is white. I would be the third owner. The seller has all the service records for all repairs and maitenance ever done on the car since it was new. He even has the factory sticker that went on the window at the dealer. The car was always garaged according to the seller. I test drove the car and it is immaculate in and out. The only defect was a scuff that removed some of the paint on the right rear corner of the car. The Kelly Bluebook list it for 4300 and that is what the seller is asking for it. Is this to much to pay for an 11 year old car?   ||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GT||10-24-1999||04:24 PM||||That price doesnt sound all that bad to me. I would definately consider it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||batboy||10-24-1999||04:56 PM||||That's one low mileage sweet sounding 88 car. Use the scuff as an excuse to offer a lower price. I bet the owner would sell that car for $4,000.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||10-24-1999||05:58 PM||||I'm going to offer the guy 3900 for it, thanks. ||||reg||1
