Z||000021||Raydar||11-03-1999||07:34 PM||||88formula... Good purchase. I'd have done it in a heartbeat. (But then, I paid 3600 for a T-Top Formula with 96000 miles, and an automatic.) Are you gonna put a V-8 in it? Or did I just misunderstand the "Mustang Killer" remark. :-) ||||reg||1
Z||000022||88formula||11-03-1999||08:32 PM||||OK, its not a mustang killer, buts its close! Maybe I'll put a 3.1 crank in it because I want to keep it as original looking as possible. I might put a turbo on it, but I'm happy with what it has for power right now. I will install those Comp Cams Magnum roller tip rockers because that is an easy 10-15% HP increase. I've never had a car before that could rip up the tires with no problem. I think the v8 engine swap is not for the fiero, its to heavy an engine and I think this would ruin the cars main strength, mainly its handling-although I could be wrong. What do you think, dose the v8 handle better with the proper suspension upgrades or dose the stock v6 fiero handle better? Which one is faster through the slalom? What condition was your formula in when you bought yours, mine was very well taken care of and had 48k miles and new tires on it. After checking out the prices on other 88 formulas in similar condition/miles I think I now got a very good deal. The person I bought it from could of asked for a lot more money and got it over time. <p>[This message has been edited by 88formula (edited 11-03-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000023||four50four||11-03-1999||10:33 PM||||two words: cadillac northstar. or is it three? anyway these things put out 300hp in the box and are lighter than the v6 and maybe even the 4. (not sure of this, just heard it somewhere)||||reg||1
Z||000024||Raydar||11-03-1999||11:27 PM||||I suspect the V-8 wouldn't handle quite as well as the 6 or 4. To be fair, I never have driven a V-8, though. My Formula was in pretty decent shape, when I bought it. Needed tires, immediately. Needs brakes. Needs a headliner (THAT'S gonna be fun.), and a paint job. It's bright red, now. Going to paint it the bright metalflake red that Lincoln/Mercury used in 99. Have another decklid with an IRM wraparound spoiler, that I'm contemplating using. Maybe a 3.4 camaro (or crate) motor. Probably ask Ed Parks to do it. He's got it down to a science. Hopefully an overdrive trans. 4T60 or Getrag. Even an Isuzu, if all else fails. <BR>I hear that Northstars are incredible in a Fiero, but for that kind of money, I could get that swimming pool installed!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000025||Standard||11-03-1999||11:52 PM||||Last I heard was the v8 swap only added something like 100 pounds, maybe less, depending on the engine used.  I don't think this would screw up the handling too much... but i'm no expert.||||reg||6
